From: Andrea Campanella <emuboy85@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libgcc: Software double for a single-float MIPS

With hard float, the MIPS libgcc builds thin C wrappers around the
hardware instructions for float and double (t-hardfp-sfdf). With
-msingle-float there are no double instructions, so a wrapper such as
__floatunsidf, whose body is "return (double) x", compiles to a call
to __floatunsidf, and every program dies in that recursion at its
first use of a double.

Keep the wrappers for float, and take the double routines and the
conversions between float and double from soft-fp, as a soft-float
build does. config.host asks the compiler whether __mips_single_float
is defined; the configure check for hard float runs before it.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [PlayStation 2 port; a candidate for upstream]
---
diff --git a/libgcc/config.host b/libgcc/config.host
index 9aa36bf..80126c8 100644
--- a/libgcc/config.host
+++ b/libgcc/config.host
@@ -165,7 +165,15 @@ mips*-*-*)
 	cpu_type=mips
 	tmake_file="mips/t-mips"
 	if test "${libgcc_cv_mips_hard_float}" = yes; then
-		tmake_file="${tmake_file} t-hardfp-sfdf t-hardfp"
+		# With -msingle-float (the R5900) the FPU has no double
+		# format: float routines wrap the hardware, double
+		# routines are software.
+		if ${CC} ${CFLAGS} -dM -E - < /dev/null 2>/dev/null \
+		   | grep -q __mips_single_float; then
+			tmake_file="${tmake_file} mips/t-hardfp-sf t-hardfp mips/t-softfp-df"
+		else
+			tmake_file="${tmake_file} t-hardfp-sfdf t-hardfp"
+		fi
 	else
 		tmake_file="${tmake_file} t-softfp-sfdf"
 	fi
diff --git a/libgcc/config/mips/t-hardfp-sf b/libgcc/config/mips/t-hardfp-sf
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f769c2b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/mips/t-hardfp-sf
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+# A single-float target (-msingle-float): the float routines wrap the
+# hardware instructions. The double routines, and the conversions
+# between float and double, come from soft-fp: see t-softfp-df.
+hardfp_float_modes := sf
+hardfp_int_modes := si
+hardfp_extensions :=
+hardfp_truncations :=
diff --git a/libgcc/config/mips/t-softfp-df b/libgcc/config/mips/t-softfp-df
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5f1b5dc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libgcc/config/mips/t-softfp-df
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# A single-float target (-msingle-float): the double routines, and the
+# conversions between float and double, are software.
+
+softfp_float_modes := df
+softfp_int_modes := si di
+softfp_extensions := sfdf
+softfp_truncations := dfsf
+softfp_exclude_libgcc2 := n
